UPDATE issues SET Rationale = '<a class=\"ballot\">Status: Rejected, 2-7, 3 No Votes</a>  \nHaving played in other FFLs, I found the uniqueness of the protections a bit refreshing from the all keeper leagues and the re-draft leagues. Having to choose each year who to keep or who let go becomes a very crucial process. It could make or break a team in come cases. There are some coaches who may like to keep a certain player(s) for whatever reason, but can\'t due to being a point or two short, and no one willing or able to trade away their protection points. Here is my proposal. A coach may protect X amount of players up to 10 max protection points over the protection point limit, but will incur a game handi-cap penalty of the amount of points equal to what the team is over.  \nExample:  \nWerewolves have used all 56 of their PP. They have 2 Defensive players they really want to keep Crayola Washington 4 Points, and Centurayon Jones 4 Points, for a toal of 8 points. That 8 points over will now be 8 points for all of the Werewolves opponents for the entire season. Every opponent will be \"spotted\" 8 points before the ball is snapped.  \n Dropping players will lower the cost of the penalty. So if the Werewolves drop Joseph Wladislaw 9 points, then the will be under the PP limit (55) and then not incur a penalty.  \nSeason to taste, but just a general idea.' WHERE IssueNum = '2013.5' AND Season = 2013 AND (Rationale IS NULL OR Rationale = '');

